if 43 over 30 is equal to a plus 1 over  B plus 1 over C plus one over D for  natural numbers a b c and d what is the  sum of a b c and d  let's work this out logically  43 over 30 is equal to 1 plus 13 over  30. take the reciprocal of the fraction  so we have 1 over 30 over 13. then 30  over 13 is equal to 2 plus 4 over 13.  substitute that in then we take the  reciprocal of the fraction so we have 1  over 13 over 4 then 13 over 4 is equal  to 3 plus 1 over 4. we substitute that  in and we have the continued fraction  representation of 43 over 30. so a plus  b plus C plus d is equal to one plus two  plus three plus four and that gives the  answer of 10.
 

